<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.1.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02340</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.1.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a0f997ad-4919-42b8-af6e-d8945e194982</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_11dde5e5-278b-4d9f-8b08-b197c7eef718" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para><emphasis>Select three</emphasis> expressions that are perfect squares.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((x+5)(x+5), (-9+c)(c−9), (a+b)(b+a)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.1.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are: \((x+5)(x+5), (-9+c)(c−9), (a+b)(b+a)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="dff1a48a-a417-4d5b-b96b-4cd06de06be8" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Each diagram represents the square of an expression or a perfect square. Complete the cells in the last
          table by answering questions a–d.</para>
          <table class="unnumbered" summary="...">
            <tgroup cols="3">
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><para>
                  <emphasis>Diagram 1</emphasis>
                   <figure>
                     <media alt="">
                       <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_10_03_10_01.png"/>
                     </media>
                   </figure>
                </para></entry>
                <entry><para>
                  <emphasis>Diagram 2</emphasis>
                   <figure>
                     <media alt="">
                       <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_10_03_10_02.png"/>
                     </media>
                   </figure>
                </para></entry>
                <entry><para>
                  <emphasis>Diagram 3</emphasis>
                   <figure>
                     <media alt="">
                       <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_10_03_10_03.png"/>
                     </media>
                   </figure>
                </para></entry>
              </row>
              </tbody>
              </tgroup>
              </table>
            <para>What is the answer for Cell a in Diagram 3?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(\frac {1}{3}h\)</para>
            <para>\(h^2\)</para>
            <para>\((\frac {1}{3}h)^2\)</para>
            <para>\((\frac {1}{3})^2\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(h^2\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.1.1 and 9.1.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(h^2\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_6412a13a-0dea-4f98-9b00-c31709c028af" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the answer for Cell b in Diagram 3?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(\frac {1}{3}h\)</para>
            <para>\(h^2\)</para>
            <para>\((\frac {1}{3}h)^2\)</para>
            <para>\((\frac {1}{3})^2\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(\frac {1}{3}h\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.1.1 and 9.1.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(\frac {1}{3}h\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8b672410-80a0-4ac7-8e1b-13019f612e3a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the answer for Cell c in Diagram 3?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(\frac {1}{3}h\)</para>
            <para>\(h^2\)</para>
            <para>\((\frac {1}{3}h)^2\)</para>
            <para>\((\frac {1}{3})^2\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(\frac {1}{3}h\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.1.1 and 9.1.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(\frac {1}{3}h\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1d8ec1dd-d88f-4ec8-805a-7ba25f5b233b" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the answer for Cell d in Diagram 3?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(\frac {1}{3}h\)</para>
            <para>\(h^2\)</para>
            <para>\((\frac {1}{3}h)^2\)</para>
            <para>\((\frac {1}{3})^2\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((\frac {1}{3})^2\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.1.1 and 9.1.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \((\frac {1}{3})^2\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_279c810f-24f4-4b34-9f36-8e0ff8d22822" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Rewrite the perfect-square expression \((n+7)^2\) in standard form \(ax^2+bx+c\).</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(16n+49\)</para>
            <para>\(n^2+14n+14\)</para>
            <para>\(n^2+49n+14\)</para>
            <para>\(n^2+14n+49\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(n^2+14n+49\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.1.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(n^2+14n+49\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_7a1a31dd-80d8-429b-9301-5b935d836307" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Rewrite the perfect-square expression \((5-m)^2\) in standard form \(ax^2+bx+c\).</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(-12m+10\)</para>
            <para>\(m^2+10m-25\)</para>
            <para>\( m^2-10m+25\)</para>
            <para>\(25m^2-10\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( m^2-10m+25\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.1.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \( m^2-10m+25\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="c040b6fe-8f55-4422-aee3-7456368c9695" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Rewrite the perfect-square expression \((h+ \frac {1}{3})^2\) in standard form \(ax^2+bx+c\).</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(2h+\frac {2}{3}h+\frac {1}{9}\)</para>
            <para>\(h^2+\frac {2}{3}h+\frac {1}{9}\)</para>
            <para>\(h^2+\frac {2}{6}h+\frac {2}{6}\)</para>
            <para>\(h^2+\frac {1}{9}h+\frac {2}{3}\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(h^2+\frac {2}{3}h+\frac {1}{9}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.1.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(h^2+\frac {2}{3}h+\frac {1}{9}\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_4146a061-87e1-445b-ad35-fb5087f2951e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For 6 - 9, solve each equation, then choose the two solutions.</para>
            <para>\((x-1)^2=4\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x= -1\) and \(x=3\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.1.3 and 9.1.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are: \(x= -1\) and \(x=3\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_62f827e1-bb1b-4c3d-9e9d-6c8c2e41b099" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\((x+5)^2=81\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x= -14\) and \(x=4\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.1.3 and 9.1.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are: \(x= -14\) and \(x=4\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="bb8157da-6f70-4865-a18d-8db84196c875" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\((x+11)^2=121\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x=0\) and \(x = -22\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.1.3 and 9.1.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are: \(x=0\) and \(x = -22\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="b2332ac2-a21f-4d65-8dce-81608a0ceb25" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\((x-7)^2=\frac {64}{49}\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x= \frac {41}{7}\) and \(x = \frac {57}{7}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.1.3 and 9.1.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are: \(x= \frac {41}{7}\) and \(x = \frac {57}{7}\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d5e71b8c-454e-4279-aef9-5790bb864ab5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter the solution to the equation.</para>
            <para>Solve the equation \((x-2)^2=0\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x=2\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.1.3 and 9.1.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(x=2\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
